{"header":{"type":"esummary","version":"0.3"},"result":{"uids":["200228188","200199813","200190604","200174284"],"200228188":{"uid":"200228188","accession":"GSE228188","gds":"","title":"NK co-culture CRISPR screen in the 721.221 B-cell lymphoblast","summary":"Therefore, to gain a deeper understanding of the interaction between NK cells and B-cell malignancies, we performed here a genome-wide CRISPR screen in the 721.221 cell line (referred to as 221), an EBV-transformed lymphoblastoid B-cell line. This cell line had been selected for the loss of classical HLA-I genes [14] and is therefore sensitive to lysis by NK cells. As expected, the loss of ligands for NK activation receptors resulted in reduced sensitivity. However, deletion of a few other genes, including Signal Peptide Peptidase-Like 3 (SPPL3), had the greatest impact on resistance to lysis by NK cells. Here, we describe how SPPL3 is a crucial controller of the interaction between NK cells and their targets. We found that the increased amount of complex N-glycans in SPPL3-deleted tumor cells limits the binding of NK cell receptors and facilitates immune evasion. We further identified glycosyl transferases that were responsible for the resistant phenotype through a secondary screen in SPPL3-deleted cells and analysis of mutations that restored sensitivity to lysis by NK cells.","gpl":"21697","gse":"228188","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Other; Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2023/03/29","suppfile":"CSV, TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM7116263","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgNT 221 cells,surviving, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116266","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgSPPL3 221 cells,surviving, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116269","title":"RNA-seq comparing sgNT 221 cells, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116272","title":"RNA-seq comparing SPPL3 knockout 221 cells, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116261","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgNT 221 cells,control, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116258","title":"221 NK killing CRISPR screen surviving, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116270","title":"RNA-seq comparing sgNT 221 cells, repeat-3"},{"accession":"GSM7116264","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgSPPL3 221 cells,control, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116267","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgSPPL3 221 cells,surviving, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116273","title":"RNA-seq comparing SPPL3 knockout 221 cells, repeat-3"},{"accession":"GSM7116256","title":"221 NK killing CRISPR screen control, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116259","title":"222 NK killing CRISPR screen surviving, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116262","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgNT 221 cells,surviving, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116265","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgSPPL3 221 cells,control, repeat-2"},{"accession":"GSM7116268","title":"RNA-seq comparing sgNT 221 cells, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116260","title":"Glycosylation secondary screen in sgNT 221 cells,control, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116271","title":"RNA-seq comparing SPPL3 knockout 221 cells, repeat-1"},{"accession":"GSM7116257","title":"222 NK killing CRISPR screen control, repeat-2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":18,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["38619967"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE228nnn/GSE228188/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA948455"},"200199813":{"uid":"200199813","accession":"GSE199813","gds":"","title":"CRISPR screens unveil signal hubs for nutrient licensing of T cell immunity [CRISPR screen]","summary":"Integrative system approaches uncover a three-tier system for the regulatory modules of nutrient signaling-dependent mTORC1 activation in primary T cells","gpl":"21103","gse":"199813","taxon":"Mus musculus","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Other","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2022/03/31","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5987795","title":"HDpS6lo1"},{"accession":"GSM5987792","title":"LDpS6hi1"},{"accession":"GSM5987801","title":"input2"},{"accession":"GSM5987798","title":"LDpS6lo2"},{"accession":"GSM5987796","title":"input1"},{"accession":"GSM5987793","title":"LDpS6lo1"},{"accession":"GSM5987799","title":"HDpS6hi2"},{"accession":"GSM5987794","title":"HDpS6hi1"},{"accession":"GSM5987797","title":"LDpS6hi2"},{"accession":"GSM5987800","title":"HDpS6lo2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":10,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["34795452"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE199nnn/GSE199813/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA821534"},"200190604":{"uid":"200190604","accession":"GSE190604","gds":"","title":"CRISPR activation and interference screens decode stimulation responses in primary human T cells [CRISPRa Perturb-seq]","summary":"Regulation of cytokine production in stimulated T cells can be disrupted in autoimmunity, immunodeficiencies, and cancer. Systematic discovery of stimulation-dependent cytokine regulators requires both loss-of-function and gain-of-function studies, which have been challenging in primary human cells. We now report genome-wide CRISPR activation (CRISPRa) and interference (CRISPRi) screens in primary human T cells to identify gene networks controlling interleukin 2 and interferon gamma production. Arrayed CRISPRa confirmed key hits and enabled multiplexed secretome characterization, revealing reshaped cytokine responses. Coupling CRISPRa screening with single-cell RNA-seq enabled deep molecular characterization of screen hits, revealing how perturbations tuned T cell activation and promoted cell states characterized by distinct cytokine expression profiles. Together, these screens reveal genes that reprogram critical immune cell functions, which could inform the design of immunotherapies.","gpl":"24676","gse":"190604","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing; Other","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2022/02/04","suppfile":"MTX, TSV, TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5726261","title":"mRNA-stim-well4"},{"accession":"GSM5726258","title":"mRNA-stim-well1"},{"accession":"GSM5726247","title":"guide-nostim-well2"},{"accession":"GSM5726246","title":"guide-nostim-well1"},{"accession":"GSM5726252","title":"guide-stim-well3"},{"accession":"GSM5726255","title":"mRNA-nostim-well2"},{"accession":"GSM5726249","title":"guide-nostim-well4"},{"accession":"GSM5726248","title":"guide-nostim-well3"},{"accession":"GSM5726251","title":"guide-stim-well2"},{"accession":"GSM5726260","title":"mRNA-stim-well3"},{"accession":"GSM5726257","title":"mRNA-nostim-well4"},{"accession":"GSM5726254","title":"mRNA-nostim-well1"},{"accession":"GSM5726253","title":"guide-stim-well4"},{"accession":"GSM5726250","title":"guide-stim-well1"},{"accession":"GSM5726256","title":"mRNA-nostim-well3"},{"accession":"GSM5726259","title":"mRNA-stim-well2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP350148","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP350/SRP350148/"}],"n_samples":16,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["35113687"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE190nnn/GSE190604/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA787633"},"200174284":{"uid":"200174284","accession":"GSE174284","gds":"","title":"CRISPR activation and interference screens decode stimulation responses in primary human T cells [Bulk RNA-seq]","summary":"Regulation of cytokine production in stimulated T cells can be disrupted in autoimmunity, immunodeficiencies, and cancer. Systematic discovery of stimulation-dependent cytokine regulators requires both loss-of-function and gain-of-function studies, which have been challenging in primary human cells. We now report genome-wide CRISPR activation (CRISPRa) and interference (CRISPRi) screens in primary human T cells to identify gene networks controlling interleukin 2 and interferon gamma production. Arrayed CRISPRa confirmed key hits and enabled multiplexed secretome characterization, revealing reshaped cytokine responses. Coupling CRISPRa screening with single-cell RNA-seq enabled deep molecular characterization of screen hits, revealing how perturbations tuned T cell activation and promoted cell states characterized by distinct cytokine expression profiles. Together, these screens reveal genes that reprogram critical immune cell functions, which could inform the design of immunotherapies.","gpl":"18573","gse":"174284","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2021/05/13","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5291008","title":"02_Donor1_sgControl_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291011","title":"05_Donor2_sgControl_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291022","title":"16_Donor4_sgFOXQ1_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291019","title":"13_Donor4_sgControl_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291017","title":"11_Donor3_sgFOXQ1_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291014","title":"08_Donor2_sgFOXQ1_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291020","title":"14_Donor4_sgControl_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291018","title":"12_Donor3_sgFOXQ1_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291021","title":"15_Donor4_sgFOXQ1_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291015","title":"09_Donor3_sgControl_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291009","title":"03_Donor1_sgFOXQ1_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291012","title":"06_Donor2_sgControl_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291016","title":"10_Donor3_sgControl_Stim"},{"accession":"GSM5291013","title":"07_Donor2_sgFOXQ1_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291007","title":"01_Donor1_sgControl_NoStim"},{"accession":"GSM5291010","title":"04_Donor1_sgFOXQ1_Stim"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP319582","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP319/SRP319582/"}],"n_samples":16,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["35113687"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE174nnn/GSE174284/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA729100"}}}
